  (text "ESD AT CONNECTORS: MOTORS U4 U5 U12-U14, EXPANSION U6 (J11)"
    (at 378.46 16.51 0)
    (effects (font (size 2 2) (thickness 0.4) (bold yes) (color 0 0 132 1)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "5412ce85-258e-48e5-bac6-61dd7f2d4cec")
  )
  (text "MOTOR SPI: fast bus, 50R on L1 over GND.\nR15/R16 (02_MCU) 30R damping, provisional.\nESD U4 U5 U12-U14 flow-through at J4-J8."
    (at 101.6 215.9 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "25e7ecd8-0e95-4389-96b0-7917d00b64da")
  )
  (text "J9 = RadioBoard2027 J2, Samtec LSHM-110-02.5 on both boards (5mm stack).\nEven row: 2 RST, 4 DATA_READY, 6 HANDSHAKE, 8 MOSI, 12 MISO, 16 SCK, 20 CS;\n10/14/18 GND. Odd row: 1/3/5 +3V3, 7-19 GND. SH to GND. Order matches U2 pins 142..132.\nFace to face, pin p here mates radio pin p+1 (odd p) or p-1 (even p).\nThe radio sits over this board on 4x M2.5 x 5mm standoffs (H5-H8).\nAll link pulls are on the radio board: R16/R17 pull HANDSHAKE/DATA_READY down, R18 holds\nCS high. With the radio absent firmware enables the STM32 internal pull-downs on PB6/PB7.\nReset is open-drain into the radio's 10k/1uF EN network (DESIGN_NOTES §11)."
    (at 151.13 302.26 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "aa0e5ac1-d940-4c5d-b873-65e38a08bb19")
  )
